# What building, testing and editing this tree leave in it. Each entry names
# something this tree's own tools produce: a broad folder name such as
# Release/, bin/ or win32/ would also hide a real source folder of that name,
# and `git add` would drop it without a word. Audio banks and WAVs are authored
# inputs, not build output, so they are tracked like any other source.

# CMake's out-of-source build trees (CMakePresets.json's binaryDir), and the
# logs tools/verify_changes.py and tools/ci_gap_report.py write beneath them.
out/

# Visual Studio's Open Folder databases and per-user settings.
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

# A developer's own presets, which CMake documents as never committed.
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Python's bytecode caches beside tools/ and its tests.
__pycache__/

# Claude Code's scratch git worktrees. Scoped to worktrees/ rather than the
# whole of .claude/, so project-level settings can still be committed.
.claude/worktrees/
